][The] IR[ATA] Level 2 Rope Access course offers a wider[ range] of knowledge and skills including[,] rigging[ working] ropes[,] undertaking a[ wider] range of resc[ues] and performing rope access tasks[.] To progress[ to] IR[ATA] Level[ 2][ candidates][ must][ have][ at][ least] 12 months and 1,[000] working[ hours] experience as an[ IR]ATA Level 1[ Technician]. Cand[idates] must[ also] have knowledge of[ legislation] and safety requirements[ relating][ to][ rope] access such as[ the] IRATA general[ requirements][.]
